{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"VERIFIED -1 ON ALL SIX AT ps2 — PROVABLY ENVIRONMENTAL, rechecked with reasoning stated.\nNOT the earlier failure and NOT a flake in the change: the job died in the CHECKOUT step, before any\ngate or test ran.\n  git fetch origin refs/changes/03/2503/2  -> couldn't find remote ref (GitHub mirror replication\n                                              had not caught up with the just-pushed patchset)\n  fallback: git fetch https://rebar.solutions.navateam.com/rebar refs/changes/03/2503/2\n                                           -> HTTP 504 after 60s, fatal: expected 'packfile'\nA server-side timeout during pack generation. Plausibly the same strain read (c) documented: the\nops sweep found /var/gerrit at 94% with repo/pack growth from 2026-08-26.\n\nRE-VERIFIED BEFORE RECHECKING rather than retrying blind, which is the whole point of the\nenvironmental carve-out:\n  refs/changes/03/2503/2, 04/2504/2, 10/2510/1 are now ALL PRESENT on the GitHub mirror, so the\n  mirror-first path resolves; and Gerrit answers HTTP 200 in 0.36s.\nPosted 'recheck' on all six with that reasoning in the comment, per AGENTS.md — recheck is reserved\nfor a provably environmental fault and the comment must state the reasoning. A flaky TEST would be a\nbug to root-cause instead; this never reached one.\n\nAlso worth noting Gerrit's own copy conditions did the right thing on the amends: it removed\nLLM-Review+1 and Verified-1 as outdated because the change was not a TRIVIAL_REBASE or\nNO_CODE_CHANGE — the amends carried real content, so the whole stack re-verifies from scratch rather\nthan inheriting stale approval."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1788330728597022001,"uuid":"d1251eb4-87fb-4b99-81b5-b67d9a97db3d"}